libsemigroups
------------------------------------------
libsemigroups is a C++ library for semigroups and monoids; it is partly based
on Algorithms for computing finite semigroups, Expository Slides, and
Semigroupe 2.01 by Jean-Eric Pin.

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.11-1
  libfmt-devel-12.2.0-1bl1
  libfmt12-12.2.0-1bl1
  libgcc1-14.4.0-1
  libsemigroups-devel-3.6.1-1bl1
  libsemigroups3-3.6.1-1bl1
  libstdc++6-14.4.0-1
  pkg-config-3.0.9-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  autoconf-20260320-3
  automake-20260320-2
  binutils-2.47-1
  cygport-0.37.10-1
  gcc-core-14.4.0-1
  gcc-g++-14.4.0-1
  libfmt-devel-12.2.0-1bl1
  libtool-2.6.2-1
  make-4.4.1-2

Canonical website:
  https://github.com/libsemigroups/libsemigroups

Canonical download:
  https://github.com/libsemigroups/libsemigroups/archive/refs/tags/v3.6.1.tar.gz

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack libsemigroups-3.6.1-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./libsemigroups-3.6.1-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/libsemigroups-3.6.1-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libsemigroups-3.6.1-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libsemigroups3-3.6.1-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libsemigroups-devel-3.6.1-X.tar.xz

-------------------------------------------

